  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Persistence / Create Account — Cloud Account", "technique": "T1136.003", "what_happened": "On 2026-05-06 at ~01:02 CEST, Wazuh's Azure AD / Entra ID audit-log module logged a UserManagement AddUser event in tenant corp.onmicrosoft.com. A new cloud account 'reportsync.20260506_010214@corp.onmicrosoft.com' (displayName 'Report Sync', department DataAnalytics, role User) was created by admin01@corp.onmicrosoft.com. The account was created accountEnabled=true with mfaEnrolled=false, with no matching IGA workflow, no HR/Workday record and no change ticket — i.e. outside any onboarding process, at ~01:00 in the morning. The service-like display name ('Report Sync') is consistent with the playbook's 'service-style naming to blend into existing account patterns' defense-evasion indicator. Wazuh fired a rule in the azure/entra rule group describing the new-account creation and attached MITRE T1136.003.", "chain_reason": "rule.groups contained the azure/entra audit group and rule.description matched the AddUser / new cloud user creation text naming reportsync.20260506_010214 and creator admin01. The univariate signature: a cloud account created out-of-hours, by a single admin, with no IGA/HR/ticket linkage and no MFA enrollment.", "first_seen": "2026-05-06T01:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Long-Term Persistence — dormancy", "technique": "T1136.003", "what_happened": "For ~7 days after creation (2026-05-06 to 2026-05-13) the reportsync account generated ZERO sign-in activity. This deliberate dormancy is the 'sleeper account' pattern: new-account monitoring typically scrutinises only the first 24-48 hours after creation, so by staying silent for a week the attacker waits out that window before activating the backdoor. The playbook explicitly lists 'accounts left unused initially' + 'legitimate login paths' as the long-term-persistence indicator set.", "chain_reason": "No sign-in / authentication alert referenced the reportsync account in the 7-day window between the AddUser event and the first observed login — the absence of activity, then a sudden first login, is itself the dormancy signature the correlation rule keys on (first_login=true AND account_age > 7d).", "first_seen": "2026-05-06T01:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts — dormant account activated from foreign IP", "technique": "T1136.003", "what_happened": "On 2026-05-13 at 08:02:14 CEST the reportsync account performed its FIRST EVER sign-in — 7 days after creation — a successful single-factor authentication (resultType=0) from callerIpAddress 185.220.101.45, geolocated to Amsterdam, NL (outside the corp known-good country set). clientAppUsed=RestApi, userAgent='python-requests/2.31.0', isInteractive=false, conditionalAccessStatus=notApplied. Wazuh fired rules in the azure/entra group for 'new account first login from Tor exit', 'dormant account reactivated foreign IP' and 'automated client first login new account', all attached to T1136.003.", "chain_reason": "An azure/entra sign-in alert referenced the reportsync account with a successful authentication whose source IP 185.220.101.45 is in the 185.220.101.0/24 Tor-exit range, with a scripted user-agent and no MFA — first_login=true on an account that is account_age > 7d is the exact dormant-account-reactivation correlation signature.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T08:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Discovery / Cloud Service & Account Enumeration via Graph", "technique": "T1136.003", "what_happened": "From 08:04 to 08:09 CEST, within seconds of the first sign-in, the reportsync account drove a burst of Microsoft Graph enumeration from the same source IP 185.220.101.45 / userAgent python-requests/2.31.0: a ListUsers call returning ~850 users, a ListGroups call returning ~120 groups, and a GetOrganization call pulling tenant metadata. This is the post-authentication reconnaissance stage — the attacker is mapping the tenant directory immediately after waking the sleeper account, exactly the playbook's Step 4 'hunt for follow-on actions' progression. Wazuh fired azure/entra alerts for the abnormal directory-enumeration volume from the new account.", "chain_reason": "azure/entra alerts referenced the reportsync account performing directory ListUsers / ListGroups / GetOrganization operations from data.srcip 185.220.101.45 in the minutes immediately after the first sign-in — bulk directory enumeration by a 7-day-old never-before-used account is the canonical attacker-recon-after-account-activation signature.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T08:04:30+0200"}
  ],
